# Line endings are decided here, not by whoever cloned the repo.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, which means git rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout. For source that is harmless. For a file whose bytes
# are pinned by a hash it is silent corruption: the file still works, but
# every recorded SHA-256 of it stops matching, and nothing says why.
#
# Meril hit this and the fix was committed as "Stop git rewriting the
# bytes of the manual". Setting it here means the next clone, on any
# machine, cannot hit it at all.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes pinned by a receipt - archify's deliver records a SHA-256 of this
# HTML and the JSON alongside it stores that hash. Treat as opaque.
docs/architecture-flow.html            -text
docs/architecture-flow.visual-check.*  -text

# Third-party payloads, vendored deliberately so the dashboard makes zero
# external requests. Not ours to reformat, and hash-pinned in the README
# beside them - a line-ending rewrite inside a .woff2 corrupts it silently
# and changes every recorded hash of a .js for no reason.
packages/core/src/jetpace_core/web/static/vendor/*  -text

# Except our own note about them, which is ours and should diff like text.
# Later rules win, so this has to stay below the line above.
packages/core/src/jetpace_core/web/static/vendor/README.md  text eol=lf

# Binary, so git should never guess.
*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
